{
  "name": "Send personalized LinkedIn connection invitations with OpenAI and Slack approval via HeyReagent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "085d5bfa-1ca7-4b32-a30a-f45eea35100f",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -760,
        -600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1200,
        "content": "## Send personalized LinkedIn connection invitations with OpenAI and Slack approval via HeyReagent\n\n### Who's it for\n\nFounders, consultants and salespeople who want to meet a certain kind of person on LinkedIn, a few a day, with a note written for each one and read by a person before it goes out.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Every weekday at 9:00 the workflow searches LinkedIn through HeyReagent's API for the people you describe: plain words and a place.\n2. For each person an OpenAI chat model writes a short invitation note from their headline and from what you say about yourself.\n3. It shows you the person and the note in Slack with two buttons. **Send it** sends the invitation from your own LinkedIn account. **Skip** leaves that person out.\n4. It pauses before the next person, so invitations do not go out in a burst.\n\nn8n's own LinkedIn node can only create posts, which is why the search and the invitation go through HTTP Request nodes.\n\n### How to set up\n\n1. Make a free account at [heyreagent.com](https://heyreagent.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template), connect your LinkedIn account, and create a key under Menu, then Developers.\n2. Create a **Bearer Auth** credential with that key and choose it in the two HTTP Request nodes.\n3. Add your **OpenAI** credential to **OpenAI Chat Model** and your **Slack** credential to **Ask me in Slack**, and pick the channel to ask in.\n4. Open **Settings**: who to look for, where, how many, what you do and why you want to connect.\n5. Run it once by hand, answer in Slack, then switch the workflow on.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- A HeyReagent account with LinkedIn connected (the free plan works)\n- An OpenAI key, or any other chat model node in its place\n- A Slack workspace\n\n### How to customize the workflow\n\n- Change the hour in **Every weekday at 9** and the search in **Settings**. One search returns at most 10 people.\n- Keep it small: HeyReagent allows 30 invitations a day per LinkedIn account (20 on a free LinkedIn account) and refuses past that. A free LinkedIn account can add a note to only a few invitations a month.\n- Swap Slack for Gmail, Telegram or Discord: their \"send and wait for response\" works the same.\n- LinkedIn's User Agreement does not allow automated activity. A person approving every invitation lowers that risk and does not remove it.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
